I don’t think Anthropic is either “evil” or “corrupt”. I haven’t heard many respectable voices making such allegations either. It seems to me that they are an extremely innovative tech company with a noble goal, a clear moral vision and incredible execution. That’s how they’ve managed to retain all the talent amidst the talent war last year that saw some leaving OpenAI.

I think Anthropic just happens to take a very specific and resolute stance on “AI safety”. We can disagree with and debate parts of their stance but I don’t question their motives. Their deep belief in safety is what has led them to be on the opposite sides of the debates on AI military use and open-source models. Dario’s antithesis to China is long-standing and well known, which extends to the open model debate. 

I think debates are good. These are not easy questions by any means. Collectively, humanity is still wrestling with these questions or being forced to anyway.

@tphuang I have met people even some senior ones at Anthropic. I’ve never met Dario but his positions are pretty well known and loudly broadcast. He doesn’t like the Chinese political system and finds it impossible to distinguish btwn the Chinese people and the China’s political system.🤷🏻‍♂️

Yes. I think Liang Wenfeng and Dario are both high-conviction AGI-pilled believers. Liang talked about the importance of “vision” for keeping everyone motivated and aligned to keep working on the mission. I think Anthropic/Dario is very much the same way. They just happen to have a very different vision.

@tphuang I think Orwellian “Big Brother” is bad in every manifestation, human or AI.

